WHY
---

Trace.lean:169    def po (_T : Transaction) (a b : Event) : Prop := a.id < b.id
                                ^^ unused

`po` ignores the transaction and is `<` on global trace positions.  AR
(Trace.lean:362) is the SAME relation between one transaction's max and
another's min.  po and AR are one relation with two names, so nothing in the
model distinguishes intra- from inter-transaction order.

AR was never proved total — only irrefl / trans / asymm.  A pending
transaction has no terminator, so it is AR-before nothing, and Ext's
"AR-latest committed setter" is not well-defined over a non-total order.

Hence: Int and Ext as stated are not the theorems we want.  Delete, rebuild.


PRINCIPLE
---------

Declarative over definitional.  Define RELATIONS, not functions.  Properties
we want should be hypotheses carried by a relation, not obligations recomputed
at each use.  Choose definitions that make the proofs easy.


